getGenElts -- general elements of an ideal cutting down the codimension
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getGenElts(I, n)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the number of general elements
        to produce
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * minTerms => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value -1, the
        minimum number of generators of I to combine when forming a general
        element; the default value -1 uses all generators
      * numCandidates => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 3,
        the number of random candidates tried at each step
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of n general elements of I

Description
===========

This function produces a list of n elements of I whose first j entries generate
an ideal of codimension j, for each j from 1 to n. Such general elements
underlie the "genElts" strategy of *note multiplicitySequence:
multiplicitySequence,.

The elements are random combinations of the generators of I, so the output
varies between runs; *note setRandomSeed: (Macaulay2Doc)setRandomSeed, makes it
reproducible.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                          |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal "xy,yz,zx";                   |
|                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : setRandomSeed 0;                        |
| -- setting random seed to 0                 |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : getGenElts(I, 2)                        |
|                                             |
|      7      7      3     5      7      3    |
|o4 = {-x*y + -x*z + -y*z, -x*y + -x*z + -y*z}|
|      9      4      4     6      8      2    |
|                                             |
|o4 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+

